        "lolChampion": "Ahri",
        "lolMentionedChampions": [
          "Ahri"
        ]
      },
      "status": "ready"
    },
    {
      "slug": "stat-growth",
      "problems": [],
      "locales": {
        "en": {
          "title": "Comparing champion stats across levels",
          "summary": "How growth changes a comparison, what base auto-attack DPS measures, and where the model stops.",
          "content": {
            "root": {
              "type": "root",
              "version": 1,
              "direction": "ltr",
              "format": "",
              "indent": 0,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "Choose the level first",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "tag": "h2"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "Champions have different base values and growth coefficients. A comparison at level one answers a different question from a comparison at level eighteen. Open ",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "version": 1,
                      "direction": "ltr",
                      "format": "",
                      "indent": 0,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "version": 1,
                          "text": "Garen versus Darius",
                          "format": 0,
                          "detail": 0,
                          "mode": "normal",
                          "style": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "fields": {
                        "linkType": "custom",
                        "url": "/compare?a=garen&b=darius",
                        "newTab": false
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": ", change the level, and inspect health, armor and attack damage separately.",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "textFormat": 0
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "RiftDen uses a nonlinear growth multiplier: (n − 1) × (0.7025 + 0.0175 × (n − 1)). It is zero at level one and seventeen at level eighteen. The increase between consecutive levels therefore changes. Attack speed can also use a separate ratio rather than the base attack speed.",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "textFormat": 0
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "Read base DPS carefully",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "tag": "h2"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "Base auto-attack DPS is attack damage multiplied by attack speed. It compares continuous basic attacks without extra effects. It excludes abilities, passives, critical strikes and items. A higher number does not establish which champion is stronger in a match.",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "textFormat": 0
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "The ",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "version": 1,
                      "direction": "ltr",
                      "format": "",
                      "indent": 0,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "version": 1,
                          "text": "duel tool",
                          "format": 0,
                          "detail": 0,
                          "mode": "normal",
                          "style": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "fields": {
                        "linkType": "custom",
                        "url": "/duel?a=garen&b=darius",
                        "newTab": false
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": " adds armor, regeneration and optional closing distance to an intentionally simplified simulation. Read its result alongside the limitations; it does not predict who wins a lane.",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "textFormat": 0
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "A practical comparison order",
                      "format": 0,
                      "detail": 0,
                      "mode": "normal",
                      "style": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "tag": "h2"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "version": 1,
                  "direction": "ltr",
                  "format": "",
                  "indent": 0,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "version": 1,
                      "text": "Pick the level at which you expect a trade. Compare health and defenses, then damage and attack speed. Check range, because the longer-ranged champion can start attacking earlier. Real gameplay also depends on abilities, spacing, items and whether either player can disengage.",
